{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146840-understanding-the-magic","id":1146840,"title":"Understanding the magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-04T16:28:20-07:00","id":1146840,"title":"Understanding the magic","content":"Trying to understand better how the magic works, cause the section on casting seems kinda abbreviated to me. Do the number of successes not count towards things like damage and how long a spell lasts, is it always 1 level of damage and one turn as a base and you have to take dice penalties to increase it? And if so do you get a number of free increases equal to something or do you have to pay for each increase regardless? Also it appears that even in combat no spell can be cast on that turn without spending one of your reach's, am I correct on this or did I miss something? And it seems like the got rid of the whole covert vulgar thing and now paradox is only risked if the storyteller feels it appropriate, am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T16:59:44-07:00","id":1146853,"title":"","content":"Number of successes affecting spell factors was a holdover from Mage the Ascension in 1ed Awakening. The only time it matters is if you need one success to successfully cast your spell or if you need 5 (or sometimes 3) to get an exceptional success. Otherwise you want to just forget about it.<br /> <br /> Yes, you have to take dice penalties to increase something along it's normal chart. Scale and Duration have advanced charts, while potency, distance, and casting time do not. They do, however, have advanced factors. ALL advanced factors (including scale and duration) require the use of a reach to take advantage of.<br /> <br /> Free increases works off of primary factor. If a spell has potency has a primary factor it allows you to increase potency BY arcanum dots minus 1 (or in other words, increase potency UP TO arcanum dots). Alternatively, if a spell has duration as primary, you can raise it along the chart a number of times BY arcanum dots minus 1 (or in other words, increase it along the chart a number of times UP TO arcanum dots). Potency and duration are the only possible primary factors.<br /> <br /> Casting time is indeed one of the five spell factors. All spells naturally have ritual speed as their casting time, thus yes you have to spend a reach to cast a spell instantly, combat situation or not. The point of the reach system is to better organize how spellcasting works in addition to give players reason to potentially cause paradox for their characters' spells. A lot of the time (though not necessarily a majority) you're not going to have enough reach to cast a spell &quot;safely,&quot; or in other words completely lacking paradox chance.<br /> <br /> Yes and no. Cover and vulgar is definitely not a thing anymore. However, no, paradox chance isn't just up to the storyteller. Rather, for every reach you spend beyond what is free you incur a number of paradox dice that is determined by your gnosis. There are other situations where you incur paradox dice, but to ensure that paradox doesn't just get completely bypassed there is now a rule that if you risk paradox you cannot reduce the number of dice lower than a chance die. Granted, a chance die isn't much, but it is still something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T03:26:53-07:00","id":1146953,"title":"","content":"The way to think about it is that instead of dice having a <i>chance</i> of granting additional potency or duration, as they do in ascension or first edition, you now <i>spend</i> them to <i>guarantee </i>it. At a cost of 2 dice per 1 guaranteed potency or whatever. Then you roll a few leftover dice (as few as you dare) to see if you manage to cast the spell or not.<br /> <br /> This means that bigger spells are harder to do, as they eat into your rolled dice budget. A high gnosis master can pull off the simplest spells almost 100% of the time. But if they really push themselves it can still blow up in their face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-05-2017, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T06:39:53-07:00","id":1147014,"title":"","content":"Is important to note that since 3 dice average 1 Success, you are better off with increasing factors by taking -2 penalties instead of fishing for Successes. An Exceptional Success can still increase the Primary Factor or offer and additional Reach, among other things, but is not something to aim for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T07:05:18-07:00","id":1147021,"title":"","content":"If you have a praxis and you're fighting against a really high withstand the 9 dice you need for decent chance at an exceptional success might mean it's better to roll than fight it directly with penalties, but that's an edge case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T13:43:16-07:00","id":1147183,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd rather not talk about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T15:08:51-07:00","id":1147216,"title":"","content":"Ok so whats the deal with primary factor whats special about it if I have to spend more dice to increase both potency and duration if duration is the primary factor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T15:14:25-07:00","id":1147220,"title":"","content":"The Primary Factor gains a bunch of free steps depending on your Arcanum dot rating.<br /> Someone casting a Potency primary spell while having 3 dots in that Arcanum will automatically gain 3 Potency instead of 1 Potency. If the same mage casts a Duration primary spell with the same Arcanum it would have a Duration of 3 turns rather than just 1 turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T15:21:52-07:00","id":1147222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146840-understanding-the-magic?p=1147216#post1147216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so whats the deal with primary factor whats special about it if I have to spend more dice to increase both potency and duration if duration is the primary factor?</div> </div> </div> </div>With an Arcana of 5 your base primary potency spell has a potency of 5 and with duration as primary a duration of 10 turns (1 year with reach with advanced). <br /> <br /> Remember you can use a reach to swap primary factors. Most of the time i wont be important but sometimes if a spell has primary of duration but you just want more potency and dont require the base duration then its sometimes worthwhile swapping the factors rather than taking alot of penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T16:00:52-07:00","id":1147228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146840-understanding-the-magic?p=1147222#post1147222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With an Arcana of 5 your base primary potency spell has a potency of 5 and with duration as primary a duration of 10 turns (1 year with reach with advanced).<br /> <br /> Remember you can use a reach to swap primary factors. Most of the time i wont be important but sometimes if a spell has primary of duration but you just want more potency and dont require the base duration then its sometimes worthwhile swapping the factors rather than taking alot of penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>So primary factor gets free increases while other factors don't? Sorry if I sound stupid but i'm coming out of 20 years of playing classic WoD so i'm just trying to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T16:07:15-07:00","id":1147230,"title":"","content":"Yes. Only the Primary Factor gains these free steps. Additionally, only Potency and Duration can be Primary Factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T17:15:49-07:00","id":1147247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146840-understanding-the-magic#post1146840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to understand better how the magic works, cause the section on casting seems kinda abbreviated to me. Do the number of successes not count towards things like damage and how long a spell lasts, is it always 1 level of damage and one <b><u><i>ritual casting time</i></u> </b>as a base and you have to take dice penalties to increase it? And if so do you get a number of free increases equal to something or do you have to pay for each increase regardless? Also it appears that even in combat no spell can be cast on that turn without spending one of your reach's, am I correct on this or did I miss something? And it seems like the got rid of the whole covert vulgar thing and now paradox is only risked if the storyteller feels it appropriate, am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also be aware that each yantra bonus after the first you use (up to your gnosis limit) adds 1 turn of casting to a spell when using reach to shorten it to one turn. So use 3 yantras and your spell takes 3 turns to cast if you use 1 reach for casting time but for base ritual casting it doesnt matter.<br /> <br /> Remember also that total Yantra's bonus is +5 but that is after taking into account penalties for spellfactors. You can take -6 for spell factors and have +11 from 5 yantra's and the total bonus is +5.<br /> <br /> You can also get +1 bonus up to 5 for each ritual casting time (based on gnosis) you add to the spell. So gnosis 1 the base it 3 hours per cast, you can add +1 for each 3 hours you extend it. (note this isnt a extended action, you make one roll at the end of the full casting time, not 1 roll per interval which ive seen some people misunderstand)<br /> <br /> But yeh i think everything else has been covered for spellcasting, theres other factors to take into account like paradox (each reach over the free you get adds dice, as does sleeper witness's and other things) and how it can mess with your spells and also withstand that you sometimes have to beat for spells to take effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T18:00:29-07:00","id":1147266,"title":"","content":"Is the free reach limit per cast or per scene, Like if i get 2 free reach's is that 2 per cast or 2 for the whole scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T18:08:07-07:00","id":1147267,"title":"","content":"Per spell. Since the spell's dot rating determines how many free Reach you get it couldn't be per scene.<br /> You gain one free Reach always plus one free Reach per Arcanum dot you have in excess of the spell's dot rating. Someone with Space 4 who tries to cast Co-location (Space 3) would have 2 free Reach.<br /> Also, if the spell is a Rote then you always calculate free Reach as if you have 5 in the relevant Arcanum. So if my example mage knows Co-location as a Rote then they have 3 free Reach instead of 2.<br /> <br /> Edit: I don't mean to be rude but it seems to me you've at most skimmed the Magic chapter. I get that the system is a bit much to wrap your head around without someone to explain it (which is why I recommend having a white-room-session before starting your campaign proper so that everyone can see the system in action and correct each other's potential misconceptions), but a more thorough reading of the chapter could preempt at least a few of your questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-05-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T18:43:18-07:00","id":1147272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146840-understanding-the-magic?p=1147267#post1147267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per spell. Since the spell's dot rating determines how many free Reach you get it couldn't be per scene.<br /> You gain one free Reach always plus one free Reach per Arcanum dot you have in excess of the spell's dot rating. Someone with Space 4 who tries to cast Co-location (Space 3) would have 2 free Reach.<br /> Also, if the spell is a Rote then you always calculate free Reach as if you have 5 in the relevant Arcanum. So if my example mage knows Co-location as a Rote then they have 3 free Reach instead of 2.<br /> <br /> Edit: I don't mean to be rude but it seems to me you've at most skimmed the Magic chapter. I get that the system is a bit much to wrap your head around without someone to explain it (which is why I recommend having a white-room-session before starting your campaign proper so that everyone can see the system in action and correct each other's potential misconceptions), but a more thorough reading of the chapter could preempt at least a few of your questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't come off rude. And I've read the magic section like 5 times, the only time I get to read though is on break at work. And I'm not sure if I'm just used to a different presentation of books than what awakening gives, but I just could't visualize it properly after reading the mechanics then reading the spells. Also I've kinda been pushed into figuring it out quickly as our group wants to try it to see the difference from ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T19:02:37-07:00","id":1147276,"title":"","content":"One of the appendices in the end of the book has a 'Spellcasting Quick Reference' that goes over the important parts. Checking it out before reading the more dense mechanics might help. Or using it as a reference point later. It's on p325.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}